WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.222
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.522 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:15.576
Unit twenty-five: Third Conditional (introduction). Today you will talk about past regrets and different results.

4
00:00:15.876 --> 00:00:18.494
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.433 --> 00:00:22.852
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.717 --> 00:00:24.776
If I had.

7
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:28.863
If I had means begins an unreal past condition.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.891
If I had studied, I would have passed.

9
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:34.880
Your turn. Say: If I had.

10
00:00:37.733 --> 00:00:38.909
If I had.

11
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:40.767
Would have.

12
00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:44.363
Would have means the result in the third conditional.

13
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:46.160
I would have passed.

14
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.356
Your turn. Say: Would have.

15
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:52.992
Would have.

16
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.204
Unreal past.

17
00:00:56.217 --> 00:00:59.656
Unreal past means a past situation that did not happen.

18
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.064
It is an unreal past.

19
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.535
Your turn. Say: Unreal past.

20
00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.854
Unreal past.

21
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:11.722
Past regret.

22
00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:15.680
Past regret means sadness about a past action.

23
00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:18.016
I feel a past regret.

24
00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:21.757
Your turn. Say: Past regret.

25
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:25.798
Past regret.

26
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:27.551
Different result.

27
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.153
Different result means what could have happened instead.

28
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.099
A different result.

29
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:36.394
Your turn. Say: Different result.

30
00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:40.594
Different result.

31
00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.305
Could have.

32
00:01:43.317 --> 00:01:45.351
Could have means a past possibility.

33
00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.183
I could have won.

34
00:01:47.783 --> 00:01:50.227
Your turn. Say: Could have.

35
00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:53.998
Could have.

36
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.681
Might have.

37
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:59.217
Might have means a weaker past possibility.

38
00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:00.992
She might have helped.

39
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:04.131
Your turn. Say: Might have.

40
00:02:06.967 --> 00:02:07.863
Might have.

41
00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:09.455
Hadn't.

42
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.450
Hadn't means the negative of had.

43
00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:14.910
If I hadn't left, I'd be there.

44
00:02:15.517 --> 00:02:17.797
Your turn. Say: Hadn't.

45
00:02:20.633 --> 00:02:21.391
Hadn't.

46
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.153
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.017 --> 00:02:29.643
Visal, tell me one decision you would change.

48
00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:41.776
If I had practised more, I would have passed the test. The third conditional talks about an unreal past: it did not happen. It describes a different result.

49
00:02:42.883 --> 00:02:43.989
How do we form it?

50
00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:56.132
If + past perfect, would have + past participle. If I had known, I would have told you. If she hadn't missed the bus, she wouldn't have been late.

51
00:02:57.217 --> 00:02:58.763
Can we use other modals?

52
00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:10.548
Yes: could have for ability or chance, might have for a weak possibility: If I had asked, he might have helped. Notice that we never put would have in the if-clause.

53
00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.165
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.017 --> 00:03:20.149
Grammar focus: Third conditional: If plus past perfect, would have plus past participle.

55
00:03:20.449 --> 00:03:21.659
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.127
If I had practised more, I would have passed.

57
00:03:26.017 --> 00:03:28.655
If she hadn't missed the bus, she wouldn't have been late.

58
00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:31.480
If I had asked, he might have helped.

59
00:03:32.433 --> 00:03:39.590
If + past perfect, would have + past participle for imaginary past situations. Never use would have in the if-clause.

60
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.920
Be careful! Don't say: If I would have known, I'd go.

61
00:03:45.867 --> 00:03:48.598
Say: If I had known, I would have gone.

62
00:03:48.898 --> 00:03:50.909
Use the past perfect after if.

63
00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.329
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:56.622
If Only I Had….

65
00:03:56.922 --> 00:03:59.966
If I had practised more, I would have passed the test.

66
00:04:00.967 --> 00:04:03.535
If I hadn't missed the bus, I wouldn't have been late.

67
00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:07.032
If I had asked for help, my friend might have helped.

68
00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:10.056
I could have won, but I made a mistake.

69
00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:14.192
A past regret is a feeling about something that cannot change.

70
00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:19.302
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.393
If I blank harder, I would have passed.

72
00:04:22.693 --> 00:04:26.382
A, studied. B, had studied. C, study.

73
00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:32.130
The answer is B: had studied.

74
00:04:33.283 --> 00:04:35.596
If she hadn't left, she blank the call.

75
00:04:35.896 --> 00:04:40.351
A, would have received. B, will receive. C, received.

76
00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.969
The answer is A: would have received.

77
00:04:47.117 --> 00:04:49.244
The third conditional talks about blank.

78
00:04:49.544 --> 00:04:53.534
A, the unreal past. B, the future. C, habits.

79
00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.483
The answer is A: the unreal past.

80
00:05:00.617 --> 00:05:01.769
Which is correct?

81
00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:09.948
A, If I would have known, I would have gone.. B, If I had known, I would have gone.. C, If I knew, I would have gone..

82
00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:16.928
The answer is B: If I had known, I would have gone..

83
00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:21.139
According to the reading, what might the friend have done?

84
00:05:21.439 --> 00:05:24.779
A, helped. B, left. C, called.

85
00:05:28.333 --> 00:05:30.019
The answer is A: helped.

86
00:05:31.233 --> 00:05:34.385
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:39.873
Write a sentence about a past decision you would change, using the third conditional.

88
00:05:48.683 --> 00:05:50.160
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:50.460 --> 00:06:03.437
If I had started learning English earlier, I would have spoken more fluently now. I wish I had practised every day. I use if + past perfect and would have + past participle.

90
00:06:03.737 --> 00:06:05.272
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:06.183 --> 00:06:13.805
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and third conditional: if plus past perfect, would have plus past participle.

92
00:06:14.105 --> 00:06:18.464
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:18.764 --> 00:06:21.973
See you in Unit twenty-six. Goodbye!

94
00:06:22.273 --> 00:06:26.853
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

